---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PrivacyNotice from '@/components/PrivacyNotice.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
import { buildSimplePageSchema } from '@/lib/schema';

const description = `Read the terms governing use of ${siteConfig.name} browser-based device tests, troubleshooting content, advertising, and third-party services.`;
const jsonLd = buildSimplePageSchema({
  type: 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms and Conditions',
  path: '/terms-and-conditions/',
  description,
  includePublisher: false,
});
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms and Conditions" description={description} canonicalPath="/terms-and-conditions/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Terms and Conditions' }]} />
  <article class="section-sm article-container prose">
    <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {siteConfig.updatedDate}</p>
    <PrivacyNotice>
      <strong>Legal note:</strong> These Terms provide general website-use rules and are not legal
      advice. They do not select an exclusive governing law or court. Mandatory rights that apply to
      you are not excluded.
    </PrivacyNotice>

    <p>
      These Terms govern your use of {siteConfig.name} at <a href={siteConfig.origin}>{siteConfig.origin}</a>,
      operated by {siteConfig.publisherName}. By using the website, you agree to these Terms. If you do
      not agree, do not use the website.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Free informational utility</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} provides free browser-based informational utilities and troubleshooting content
      for webcams, microphones, speakers and headphones, keyboards, mice and trackpads, touchscreens,
      displays, refresh timing, browser capabilities, game controllers, and pre-call readiness. The
      launch site does not require a paid subscription or user account.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Informational purpose only</h2>
    <p>
      The tests provide browser-based observations and user-guided checks. They are not professional
      hardware certification, manufacturer diagnostics, laboratory calibration, medical advice, legal
      advice, safety certification, accessibility certification, employment advice, warranty
      determination, or proof that a device is free from defects.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No warranty of exact results</h2>
    <p>
      Results can be affected by browser behavior, operating-system settings, permissions, hardware,
      drivers, scaling, zoom, network conditions, other applications, user confirmation, accessibility
      software, organization policy, and device routing. A browser result may differ from a third-party
      application.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Local processing and permissions</h2>
    <p>
      Primary test media and interactions are designed to run locally. You control whether to grant
      browser permissions. Stop or exit a test when finished. Do not monitor another person, use a
      device without authorization, or type sensitive information in the keyboard test.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Safe use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use a low comfortable speaker volume.</li>
      <li>Follow manufacturer cleaning, electrical, battery, display, and repair guidance.</li>
      <li>Do not use flashing or aggressive pixel-repair content from untrusted sources.</li>
      <li>Do not rely solely on the site for safety-critical, medical, employment, examination, legal, financial, or warranty decisions.</li>
      <li>Seek qualified service when physical damage, overheating, electrical risk, or persistent failure is suspected.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Availability and compatibility</h2>
    <p>
      The website does not guarantee support for every browser, device, assistive technology,
      operating system, or third-party platform. Features may be unavailable when a browser lacks an
      API, the page is not secure, a permission is blocked, or an organization policy applies.
    </p>

    <h2>7. User responsibility</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the website lawfully and follow instructions.</li>
      <li>Select appropriate devices and safe volume levels.</li>
      <li>Protect passwords and sensitive information.</li>
      <li>Avoid sensitive input during the keyboard test.</li>
      <li>Verify important results through another method.</li>
      <li>Confirm third-party platform requirements.</li>
      <li>Decide whether equipment requires professional service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Prohibited misuse</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Unlawful use or attempts to damage, disrupt, probe, or bypass website security.</li>
      <li>Introducing malware or excessive automated requests.</li>
      <li>Misusing camera, microphone, screen-sharing, or input permissions.</li>
      <li>Monitoring another person without permission.</li>
      <li>Misrepresenting results as professional certification.</li>
      <li>Facilitating fraud, abuse, harassment, or unauthorized surveillance.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Unless stated otherwise, original text, design, branding, code, interface copy, and
      troubleshooting structure are owned by or licensed to {siteConfig.publisherName} and protected
      by applicable law. Open-source dependencies remain subject to their own licenses. Third-party
      names and trademarks belong to their owners and do not imply endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Feedback and contact submissions</h2>
    <p>
      You may submit suggestions, bug reports, corrections, privacy questions, or accessibility
      feedback through the Contact page. Form submissions are processed by FormSubmit and email
      providers. Do not submit confidential or proprietary information. The publisher is not required
      to implement every suggestion.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The website may later display Google AdSense advertising to support free access. Advertisers do
      not determine device-test results, pass or failure states, editorial conclusions, or
      troubleshooting recommendations. Transactions are between the visitor and advertiser.
      Advertising is disabled at launch.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Third-party services and links</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses or may link to hosting providers, FormSubmit, email providers, browser vendors,
      operating-system providers, manufacturers, meeting platforms, advertisers, and other third
      parties. The publisher is not responsible for their availability, security, privacy practices,
      products, services, pricing, support, or claims.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Service changes</h2>
    <p>
      The publisher may update tests, correct content, remove a feature, change hosting, introduce or
      remove advertising, change supported browsers, or perform maintenance. Continuous or error-free
      access is not guaranteed.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Disclaimer of warranties and liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, the website is provided “as is” and “as available.”
      The publisher does not warrant that every result will be exact, every problem will be found,
      every fix will work, or every third-party platform will function. Nothing in these Terms excludes
      rights or warranties that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms do not designate an exclusive governing law, court, or dispute forum. Applicable
      mandatory law and consumer rights may depend on where you live and the circumstances of your use.
      Contact {siteConfig.legalEmail} with a legal notice or question.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
